1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,052
Paying the minimum due feels

2
00:00:02,072 --> 00:00:02,417
smart.

3
00:00:02,437 --> 00:00:03,825
It's the most expensive

4
00:00:03,845 --> 00:00:05,376
button on your card.

5
00:00:05,396 --> 00:00:06,941
Most Indian credit cards

6
00:00:06,961 --> 00:00:08,561
charge up to three point

7
00:00:08,581 --> 00:00:10,589
seven five percent a month.

8
00:00:10,609 --> 00:00:11,736
That's about forty-five

9
00:00:11,756 --> 00:00:12,861
percent a year.

10
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:14,629
Say you owe one lakh rupees,

11
00:00:14,649 --> 00:00:16,450
and you only pay the minimum,

12
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,894
about five percent.

13
00:00:17,914 --> 00:00:19,037
After twelve months,

14
00:00:19,057 --> 00:00:20,578
you've paid around fifty-six

15
00:00:20,598 --> 00:00:21,375
thousand.

16
00:00:21,395 --> 00:00:22,698
And you still owe about

17
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:23,956
eighty-six thousand.

18
00:00:23,976 --> 00:00:24,367
Worse,

19
00:00:24,387 --> 00:00:26,190
new purchases usually lose

20
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:28,194
their interest-free period.

21
00:00:28,214 --> 00:00:29,712
The minimum due only saves

22
00:00:29,732 --> 00:00:30,803
you from late fees.

23
00:00:30,823 --> 00:00:32,526
It doesn't clear the debt.

24
00:00:32,546 --> 00:00:34,140
This assumes three point

25
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,921
seven five percent a month

26
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:37,702
and a five percent minimum.

27
00:00:37,722 --> 00:00:39,616
Real terms vary by bank.

28
00:00:39,636 --> 00:00:41,006
So pay the total due.

29
00:00:41,026 --> 00:00:41,807
If you can't,

30
00:00:41,827 --> 00:00:43,357
pay as much as you can,

31
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:44,726
and stop swiping.

32
00:00:44,746 --> 00:00:47,206
Follow The 7% Club.
